A||||22||RiceCooker||Manual Transmission Question ........please||||1||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||03-30-2001||05:23 PM||||OK, my car is an 86SE V6 4spd<P>Since i can remember, my car has always been tough to get into 1st and it grinds a little to get in reverse. <BR>Well today at lunch it gets severly worse.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I can't even get into first. Second is tough but i can manage. Even 3rd and 4th are pretty stiff. <BR>With the car off, i can shift through the gears perfectly smooth.<P>I have done a search and i am currently reading the superlong clutch thread. However i do not think that it is clutch related because i have a small leak from my Transmission. I am not exactly sure where its leaking from because i havent checked it out yet, but its on the left side. I will have to see if i can find out where its leaking from.<P>Could a lack of tranny fluid be the cause of the problem. It was a bit stiff last night and fine this morning. I took it out for lunch and it was OK until i was driving for about 15 mins or so then it just got REALLY BAD.<BR>If it's just tranny fluid, where can if add fluid just to check it out.<P>Any info would be greatly appreciated. I just had it in the shop fixing my never ending coolant problems but it's all taken care of and now this.<P>Thanks,<BR>Todd||||reg||1
Z||000001||N_Man||03-30-2001||06:17 PM||||Todd<BR>My first thought was a clutch problem, but if your confident it isnt.  Where does the clutch find the friction point? Is it just off the floor?  Or is in normal?<P>My second thought is LOW oil level in the trans.  Just unscrew the spedo sensor and it should ave a level marker on it.  Also 5w30 is cheap enough and easy enough to change to see if it helps.<P>Neal||||reg||1
Z||000002||phreakboy4||03-30-2001||06:22 PM||||it really doesnt sound like its your transmission The way your describing it, I think that it is the clutch since you say that it engages just fine when not running it sounds like the clutch isnt disengaging<P>84 2M4 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000003||862M4inCA||03-30-2001||06:29 PM||||I'll have to agree with a clutch problem. If it was a lack of lubrication in the tranny then it should be stiff to shift either running or not (parts showing early signs of seizure). Also when you mention difficulty and grinding when going into reverse suggests the clutch isn't fully disengaging. I think after filling the tranny up with oil you should find that the "original" stiff 1st and reverse will still be present and suggest a clutch replacement for that. As for the other gears being stiff, that's sounds like a lack of lubricant.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||03-30-2001||06:32 PM||||Hey Todd<BR>Give me a call - we can check it out.  I went through HELL with my '85 trying to get the tranny to shift smooth.  I've learned a few things, though.  Maybe one of them could be useful here!<BR>Voytek||||reg||1
Z||000005||RiceCooker||03-30-2001||06:33 PM||||Thanks guys<P>Im at work but i jus went down into the parkade and checked it. The clutch pedal seemd to have a bit of "play" and i dont think its supposed to. So it's in reverse (car shut off) And i press in the clutch and start the car and i totally start moving backwards.<P>SO IT'S THE CLUTCH<P>bad news though. I have to shut off the car to get in and out of any gear so it doesnt look like ill be making it home. That really stinks. ||||reg||13
