Z||000010||stsmithgt||03-30-2001||07:12 PM||||Here's an idea...I had a similar problem.  It turned out to be a shift cable needed to be adjusted.  First gear became a lot easier to get in and I could shift into 2nd without grinding it when zipping onto the highway.  I suppose my cable had some slack in it because my reverse lights wouldn't stay on.  I took my console out and studied the linkage there and on the tranny.  I could see it wasn't staying engaged to the reverse light switch.  It's nice when the problem is a simple one.  The book helps a little.  It kept my beer from tipping over on the seat. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
